A||||2||DaveL||Engine Stand Question||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||10-25-2001||07:51 AM||||I have bought a used 2.5 and am getting ready to work on it before installing it, and I'm having trouble getting it on my engine stand. There are sleeves sticking out about a half inch from 2 of the mounting holes on the block, to align the tranny I assume. This engine came from a Celebrity, I believe. Anyway, they are making it difficult to get the mount for the stand bolted to it. Do these come out? Are they removable? Maybe they are peculiar to the Celebrity?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-25-2001||09:19 AM||||I had similar sleeves on a Suzuki Samurai motor.  They were removable but wedged in pretty good.  I suspect these are the same.<BR>If not you may need spacers to offset the other bolts evenly on the stand.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||10-25-2001||01:02 PM||||Those pins are required to align the engine to the bellhousing. Fiero engines have them also. They will come out, but are press fit so it's hard to get them out and back in without bending them.<P>Go to the hardware store and get some big washers to use for spacers. I usually put the washers around the pins too so they don't get bent. You may need longer bolts too depending on how the stand is made.||||reg||1
